On March 19, 2026, Frank Mittelbach, long-time \LaTeX\ team
leader, received an honorary doctorate.
The Faculty of Informatics, Masaryk University, has recognized
his profound contributions in the document
and software engineering areas of Computer Science,
and submitted a proposal to the university's scientific senate
based on Frank's achievements and qualities.
And the senate approved it!

This paper summarizes the reasoning behind this choice and
reports on related events that happened in Brno,
linking them to the honorary doctorate of Masaryk University
from 1996, when the recipient was Donald Knuth.
